<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antônio de Sousa Neto</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1803">1803</a>–<a href="/years/1866">1866</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antônio de Sousa Neto was a gaúcho general of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ragamuffin-war">Ragamuffin War</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>. After his victory at Seival on 10 September 1836 he proclaimed the Riograndense Republic the next day. He later fought for Brazil in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paraguayan-war">Paraguayan War</a> and died of wounds in 1866.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antonio-de-sousa-neto.jpg" alt="Antônio de Sousa Neto" width="320" height="380" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Azevedo Dutra · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MuseuJulio9.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
